// endpoint_subscribe_slack_thread.proto — SubscribeSlackThread: tell one
// workspace's agent about a Slack thread's new messages, as digests. AGENT API
// section. How the daemon reads the thread, batches its messages and keeps the
// workspace's own posts from being told back is slack_thread.proto's header.
//
// WHAT A SUBSCRIBE DOES. It resolves the link to the thread's root, makes sure
// the channel is routed into the user's echo pipe, and starts the cursor at the
// pipe's head, so only messages written after the subscription are told. A
// fresh subscription announces itself in the thread, naming the workspace and
// its mode; subscribing again changes the mode only, keeps the cursor and
// announces nothing unless the mode changed.

